  "unit": "u11-plans",
  "title": "He'll, she'll, they'll",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**He, she and they** use endings you already know:\n\n- সে / ও / তারা → **-বে**: **সে আসবে** 'he'll come', **তারা আসবে** 'they'll come'\n- তিনি / উনি (polite) → **-বেন**: **উনি আসবেন**\n\nSo **-বে** is both 'you (তুমি) will' and 'he/she will', and **-বেন** is both polite 'you' and polite 'he/she'. The pronoun or the context tells you who.\n\n**Vowel change:** in the future, **এ** and **ও** in a stem rise to **ই** and **উ**, as in the আমি present: কেনা → **কিনবে**, শোনা → **শুনবে** (শুনি), ওঠা → **উঠবে** (উঠি). Start from the আমি form and swap the ending.",
